<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomasites</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thomasites were American teachers sent to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> in the early years of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> rule, named after the transport ship USAT Thomas, which brought over five hundred of them in 1901. They set up a public school system teaching in English and trained Filipino teachers. Their work made English widely spoken in the Philippines.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomasites.jpg" alt="Thomasites" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sharlyne Ang and Karla Redor · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WTMP_Foodtrippings_D19.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
